# Two errors inside one string are reported in source order.
mode: syntax
---- query
from t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..31
  PIPELINE@0..30
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    WHERE_OP@9..30
      IDENT@9..14 "where"
      WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
      BIN_EXPR@15..30
        NAME_REF@15..16
          IDENT@15..16 "s"
        WHITESPACE@16..17 " "
        EQ2@17..19 "=="
        WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
        LITERAL@20..30
          STRING@20..30 "'\\q\\u{zz}'"
  WHITESPACE@30..31 "\n"

error[DS0005]: unknown escape sequence `\q`
  --> query:1:22
  |
1 | from t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
  |                      ^^ not a valid escape
  |
  = help: to write a backslash, double it: `'\\q\u{zz}'`
  = note: valid escapes are `\\`, `\"`, `\'`, `\n`, `\r`, `\t`, `\0` and `\u{...}`

error[DS0005]: invalid unicode escape `\u{zz}`
  --> query:1:24
  |
1 | from t | where s == '\q\u{zz}'
  |                        ^^^^^^ not a valid unicode escape
  |
  = help: write `\u{` followed by 1 to 6 hex digits and `}`, e.g. `\u{1F600}`
